{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>An oracle. The word of HaShem</b> — Hadrach is the name of a human kingdom or the name of a king. And the resting place of the oracle is in Damascus, for there too this prophecy, attached to the Second Temple, will be fulfilled." "And the sense of <b>for to HaShem is the eye of man</b> — that many of the people of Damascus return to worship HaShem and submit to the authority of Israel, who were in Jerusalem, namely Judah and Benjamin and those who returned from Assyria, as written in Ezra, for HaShem made them joyful and turned the heart of the king of Assyria." "The prefixed ל of לַיהוה serves in place of another, like the prefixed מ of מֵאֵל אָבִיךָ, which serves in place of another מ. And [so] אֶת שַׁדַּי and מֵאֵת שַׁדַּי. And so it is: <b>and all the tribes of Israel, their eyes are to there</b> — to serve Him and [to follow] what Israel teaches them."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {2 "The second half of comment [2] is textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing. The transition from grammatical analogy to the verse interpretation is abrupt and possibly corrupt in the witnesses."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:31.212546309Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}